---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Sound Evidence — educational companion site, evidence labels, and disclaimer."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>About Sound Evidence</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Sound Evidence is a static companion library for people curious about music, sound practices,
        and wellbeing research. It is <strong>not</strong> a sales site, not a Meta Musician clone,
        and not a clinic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What we are</h2>
      <p>
        An educational layer that paraphrases publicly available reviews and institutional briefs —
        especially Cochrane, NCCIH, and open-access papers we could read in full — so readers can see
        strength-of-evidence differences at a glance.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Educational only — not medical advice.</strong> Nothing on this site diagnoses,
          treats, cures, or prevents any disease. Do not change medications or care plans based on
          these summaries. Talk with a qualified clinician for personal health decisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Evidence labels</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strong / mixed→strong:</strong> careful systematic reviews with moderate-or-better certainty for a defined short-term adjunct outcome.</li>
        <li><strong>Mixed:</strong> real signals with low certainty, high heterogeneity, fading effects, or subjective/objective mismatch.</li>
        <li><strong>Weak:</strong> uncontrolled designs, tiny samples, or high risk of bias across trials (singing bowls; VAT pain literature).</li>
        <li><strong>None for medical claims:</strong> cure language, 432/528-as-medicine mythology, unsupported energy-field mechanisms.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>FTC-safe posture</h2>
      <p>
        We prefer <em>adjunct</em> and <em>short-term</em> wording. Singing bowls stay in the weak column.
        We do not equate vibroacoustic 40 Hz device research with crystal-bowl sound baths.
        Licensed music therapy is kept distinct from wellness sound practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Related project</h2>
      <p>
        Soft credit: related to
        <a href="https://themetamusician.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Meta Musician</a>
        — an education project about sound and musicianship. This hub does not hard-sell courses.
      </p>

      <h2>Palette</h2>
      <p class="small muted">
        Brand orange <code>#df4633</code> · cream cards <code>#e7e1d2</code> · page cream <code>#f1ede8</code> ·
        terracotta <code>#ce523e</code> · ink <code>#2A221C</code> · muted <code>#6B5E54</code>.
        Headings: Manrope. Body: Karla. Accent script: Sloop Script One where licensed, falling back to Great Vibes (Google Fonts).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
